# CatInheritanceCharge — Ireland Capital Acquisitions Tax charge (CATCA 2003)

The Capital Acquisitions Tax (CAT) charge on one beneficiary's taxable benefit under an
inheritance, per the Capital Acquisitions Tax Consolidation Act 2003 (CATCA 2003). Unlike UK
Inheritance Tax (`IhtDeathCharge.catala_en`), CAT is **beneficiary-side**: the accountable
person is the successor/donee (CATCA 2003 s.45), and the charge is computed per (beneficiary x
benefit), not once on the aggregate estate. A beneficiary-side scope therefore takes one
invocation per beneficiary's benefit, in contrast to `IhtDeathCharge`'s single estate-aggregate
invocation — the incidence axis this contrast motivates is machine-readable in the jurisdiction
parameter layer (`linkml/parameters/parameters.yaml` `TaxIncidenceEnum`), not in Catala.

The scope returns the `ComputedOrNeedsHuman.Verdict` contract (doctrine §1a; Constitution
Principle XIII): a definite legal figure travels in the `Computed` arm.

Legal-correctness is asserted **outside this file** by the T032 gov-oracle harness (TT-478):
`code-inherit-test-suite/scripts/oracle_verify.py` runs this scope and checks the computed
figure against the published revenue.ie figure cited in
`tests/oracles/ie-cat-charge.oracle.json`. This file therefore carries the law, not its own
assertions.

(Prose note: a line must not begin with the reserved `>` directive prefix, so any statutory
quotation is kept inline.)

Statutory figures (current values; live-sourced revenue.ie 2026-07-02 — Budget 2026 confirmed
no change to CAT thresholds):

- Group A threshold (parent to child) = €400,000
- Group B threshold (e.g. sibling, niece/nephew, grandchild) = €40,000
- Group C threshold (all other relationships) = €20,000
- rate = 33% on the taxable value above the relevant group threshold
- lifetime aggregation of same-group benefits received since 5 December 1991 (CATCA 2003 Sch 2
  para 3) — `prior_same_group_benefits` is a required input because omitting it computes the
  wrong tax
- spouse/civil partner transfers are fully exempt (CATCA 2003 s.70/s.71)

Group **classification** from kinship (which threshold a beneficiary falls under) is
out-of-scope here — supplied by the caller/projection; CATCA 2003 Sch 2 Pt 1 edge cases (e.g. a
minor child of a predeceased child) are `NeedsHuman` territory in Phase-alpha. Dwelling-house
relief (s.86), agricultural relief (s.89), and business relief (s.92) are not computed by this
rule — a relief claim routes to `NeedsHuman` (`relief_claimed`).

The group thresholds and the rate are `context` parameters (ICP-A1) whose authoritative values
live in the jurisdiction parameter layer; the literals below are the overridable defaults.

G6 certification floor (TT-427/TT-1079): every input is a characterisation judgement
(`registry/governance-layers.yaml`, all L3 — the benefit valuations, the CAT-group
kinship classification, spousehood, and the relief claim), so each arrives as a
`Certified<Type> | NotCharacterised` enum; any uncertified input routes `NeedsHuman`
via the `uncertified_inputs` gate. `CertifiedCatGroup` is declared HERE (not in the
shared contract module) because `CatGroup` is this module's own classification enum
and the contract module cannot import rule modules — the rule-local twin the contract
module's certification-floor note describes.

```catala
declaration enumeration CatGroup:
  -- GroupA
  -- GroupB
  -- GroupC

declaration enumeration CertifiedCatGroup:
  -- Certified content CatGroup
  -- NotCharacterised

declaration scope Charge:
  input taxable_benefit content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney
  input prior_same_group_benefits content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney
  input cat_group content CertifiedCatGroup
  input spouse_or_civil_partner content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool
  input relief_claimed content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool
  context group_a_threshold content money
  context group_b_threshold content money
  context group_c_threshold content money
  context cat_rate content decimal
  internal uncertified_inputs content boolean
  internal taxable_benefit_v content money
  internal prior_same_group_benefits_v content money
  internal cat_group_v content CatGroup
  internal spouse_or_civil_partner_v content boolean
  internal relief_claimed_v content boolean
  internal threshold content money
  internal available_threshold content money
  internal taxable_excess content money
  internal tax content money
  output verdict content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.Verdict

scope Charge:
  definition group_a_threshold equals $400,000
  definition group_b_threshold equals $40,000
  definition group_c_threshold equals $20,000
  definition cat_rate equals 0.33
  definition uncertified_inputs equals
    (match taxable_benefit with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match prior_same_group_benefits with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match cat_group with pattern -- CertifiedCatGroup.Certified content v: false -- CertifiedCatGroup.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match spouse_or_civil_partner with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match relief_claimed with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: true)
  # certified-value extractions — fallbacks are dead code (verdict routes first)
  definition taxable_benefit_v equals
    match taxable_benefit with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: $0
  definition prior_same_group_benefits_v equals
    match prior_same_group_benefits with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: $0
  definition cat_group_v equals
    match cat_group with pattern -- CertifiedCatGroup.Certified content v: v -- CertifiedCatGroup.NotCharacterised: GroupC
  definition spouse_or_civil_partner_v equals
    match spouse_or_civil_partner with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: false
  definition relief_claimed_v equals
    match relief_claimed with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: false
  definition threshold equals
    match cat_group_v with pattern
    -- GroupA: group_a_threshold
    -- GroupB: group_b_threshold
    -- GroupC: group_c_threshold
  definition available_threshold equals
    if threshold > prior_same_group_benefits_v
    then threshold - prior_same_group_benefits_v
    else $0
  definition taxable_excess equals
    if taxable_benefit_v > available_threshold
    then taxable_benefit_v - available_threshold
    else $0
  definition tax equals taxable_excess * cat_rate
  definition verdict equals
    if uncertified_inputs then NeedsHuman
    else if spouse_or_civil_partner_v then Computed content $0
    else (if relief_claimed_v then NeedsHuman else Computed content tax)
```
